<article class="env-lemma" id="0EFS">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0EFS">Lemma <span data-tag="0EFS">115.4.16</span>.</a> Let $(A, \mathfrak m)$ be a Noetherian local ring. Let $I \subset A$ be an ideal. Let $M$ be a finite $A$-module. Let $s$ and $d$ be integers. Assume </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li class="custom-item" data-marker="(a)"><p>
$A$ has a dualizing complex, 
</p>
</li><li class="custom-item" data-marker="(b)"><p>
$\text{cd}(A, I) \leq d$, 
</p>
</li><li class="custom-item" data-marker="(c)"><p>
if $\mathfrak p \not\in V(I)$ then $\text{depth}_{A_\mathfrak p}(M_\mathfrak p) > s$ or $\text{depth}_{A_\mathfrak p}(M_\mathfrak p) + \dim (A/\mathfrak p) > d + s$. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
  <p> Then the assumptions of Algebraic and Formal Geometry, Lemma <a href="/tag/0EFR" data-tag="0EFR">52.10.4</a> hold for $A, I, \mathfrak m, M$ and $H^ i_\mathfrak m(M) \to \mathop{\mathrm{lim}}\nolimits H^ i_\mathfrak m(M/I^ nM)$ is an isomorphism for $i \leq s$ and these modules are annihilated by a power of $I$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      The assumptions of Algebraic and Formal Geometry, Lemma <a href="/tag/0EFR" data-tag="0EFR">52.10.4</a> by the more general Algebraic and Formal Geometry, Lemma <a href="/tag/0EFW" data-tag="0EFW">52.10.5</a>. Then the conclusion of Algebraic and Formal Geometry, Lemma <a href="/tag/0EFR" data-tag="0EFR">52.10.4</a> gives the second statement. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>